WiseOwl COBOL 31.0.0  ANSI X3.23-1985 (--std 85)  P5980E  2026-11-20 21:51:25 -08:00                                          PAGE 2
SOURCE  conformance-suite/cases/X.1.3.8@1985-Scope-of-Names/pb5980-own-data-item-hides-global-record-entry-write-85.cob

                 ----+----1----+----2----+----3----+----4----+----5----+----6----+----7----+----8
     1  *              *>--- conformance-case
     2  *              *> id: pb5980-own-data-item-hides-global-record-entry-write-85
     3  *              *> rules: [1985-GR-X.1.3.8.2-3]
     4  *              *> source-format: fixed
     5  *              *> portable: unverified
     6  *              *>---
     7  *              *> kb/Work PB5980 (review R1-1). A refusal at 85. §1985:X.1.3.8.2 GR3a (ci
        +        te.py:
     8  *              *> OK): "If the name is declared in program B, the object in
     9  *              *> program B is the referenced object." The container's FD F has no
    10  *              *> GLOBAL clause but its level-1 entry FR does, so FR is a GLOBAL
    11  *              *> record-name; the contained program declares
    12  *              *> its own data item FR. WRITE FR there names that data item, so it
    13  *              *> is no logical record and is refused (COBOL1757); the refusal names
    14  *              *> the hiding data item and the GLOBAL record-name it hides, never
    15  *              *> that no file description entry has such a record.
    16                  IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
    17                  PROGRAM-ID. P5980E.
    18                  ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
    19                  INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
    20                  FILE-CONTROL.
    21                      SELECT F ASSIGN TO "p5980e.dat".
    22                  DATA DIVISION.
    23                  FILE SECTION.
    24                  FD  F.
    25                  01  FR  GLOBAL PIC X(3).
    26                  PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    27                  MAIN-1.
    28                      CALL "P5980EJ".
    29                      STOP RUN.
    30                  IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
    31                  PROGRAM-ID. P5980EJ.
    32                  DATA DIVISION.
    33                  WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
    34                  01  FR  PIC X(3) VALUE "DDD".
    35                  PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    36                  B-1.
    37                      WRITE FR.
                            ^
                 ==> error COBOL1757 (col 12): WRITE 'FR' — record-name-1 "is the name of a logical record in the file section of
                     the data division and may be qualified" (ISO §1985:VII.4.7.3 SR2, §1985:VIII.4.9.3 SR2, §1985:IX.4.9.3 SR2);
                     'FR' here names a data item declared at line 34 in this program, which hides the GLOBAL record-name 'FR' of a
                     containing program (ISO §1985:X.1.3.8.2 GR3a: "If the name is declared in program B, the object in program B is
                     the referenced object"), so 'FR' is not a logical record of a file description entry visible here. Rename one
                     of the two declarations.
    38                      EXIT PROGRAM.
    39                  END PROGRAM P5980EJ.
    40                  END PROGRAM P5980E.
    41
